---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy notice — deployment draft" description="Privacy notice — deployment draft" lang="en">
<main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16"><a href="/" class="text-indigo-600">Signalist</a><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-10">Privacy notice — deployment draft</h1>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Operator</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">This notice describes the software defaults. Before public launch, the deployment operator must publish its legal identity, contact address, applicable legal bases, hosting locations, subprocessors and backup retention. These details have not been supplied for this repository.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Data and purposes</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Signalist stores account email, a password hash, optional display name, RSS sources and articles, bookmarks and notes, team memberships and annotations, consent history and minimal access events. Connected accounts store encrypted authorization material. These records support authentication, reading, collaboration, requested synchronization and approved publication.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Your controls</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Settings allow you to export your own data, change your display name, grant or withdraw optional consent, restrict processing, and request deletion with password confirmation. Active subscriptions must be cancelled and sole workspace administrators must transfer administration first. Team content may remain with other members; your annotations and membership are erased and attribution is anonymized.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Optional external services</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">External AI is disabled until a provider is configured. When enabled with consent, article text is cleaned and common identifiers and known names are minimized before processing. This filter is not a guarantee of complete anonymization. Private bookmark notes are excluded from AI prompts. Raindrop note sync is opt-in. Social publishing sends only the approved post text to the selected connected provider. Payment pages are hosted by Stripe when configured.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Retention</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">The optional daily policy removes articles older than 90 days only when neither personal nor shared bookmarks retain them. Expired authorization attempts and SDK sessions are purged, unconfirmed waitlist requests expire after seven days, and access events and account tombstones expire after 30 days. The operator must enable this policy and define retention for backups and service logs; it is disabled by default.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Waitlist and analytics</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">A waitlist request records email and consent and requires email confirmation. The confirmation message also contains a withdrawal link. Landing analytics are off unless the operator supplies a Plausible script URL. Analytics do not receive account IDs, article text, email fields or application content from this implementation.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Requests and complaints</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Use the deployment operator’s published contact for requests that cannot be completed in Settings, recipient or backup deletion, and information about the relevant supervisory authority. This draft must be completed before public collection of personal data.</p></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
